@startuml sequence_diagram

actor User
participant CalculatorCLI
participant CalculatorService
participant MemoryService
participant HistoryExportService
participant StatisticsService
participant FilterService
participant Calculator
participant JsonStorage

== Unary Operation Flow (Scientific Mode) ==
User -> CalculatorCLI: selects unary operation (sin, cos, tan, log, ln, exp, sqrt, square)
activate CalculatorCLI

note over CalculatorCLI: operation.is_unary() returns true\nonly asks for one operand

CalculatorCLI -> CalculatorService: perform(operation, a, None)
activate CalculatorService

note over CalculatorService: b parameter is None\nperform_with_memory() handles None gracefully

CalculatorService -> Calculator: calculate(operation, a, 0)
activate Calculator
Calculator --> CalculatorService: result
deactivate Calculator

note over CalculatorService: operands = [a] (only one operand)\noperand_b is None in CalculationResult

CalculatorService --> CalculatorCLI: CalculationResult with operand_b=None
deactivate CalculatorService

CalculatorCLI -> User: shows result as "sin(a) = r"
deactivate CalculatorCLI

== Binary Operation Flow (Standard & Scientific Mode) ==
User -> CalculatorCLI: selects binary operation (add, subtract, multiply, power, modulo)
activate CalculatorCLI

note over CalculatorCLI: operation.is_unary() returns false\nasks for two operands

CalculatorCLI -> CalculatorService: perform(operation, a, b)
activate CalculatorService

note over CalculatorService: start_time = perf_counter()

CalculatorService -> Calculator: calculate(operation, a, b)
activate Calculator
Calculator --> CalculatorService: result
deactivate Calculator

note over CalculatorService: end_time = perf_counter()\ncreate CalculationResult with execution_time_ms

CalculatorService -> JsonStorage: save(memory_entry)
activate JsonStorage
JsonStorage --> CalculatorService: saved
deactivate JsonStorage

CalculatorService --> CalculatorCLI: CalculationResult with operand_b value
deactivate CalculatorService

CalculatorCLI -> User: shows result as "a op b = r"
deactivate CalculatorCLI

== Mode Toggle Flow ==
User -> CalculatorCLI: selects mode toggle option from menu
activate CalculatorCLI

CalculatorCLI -> CalculatorCLI: _toggle_mode()

note over CalculatorCLI: if mode == "standard": switch to "scientific"\nupdate _menu to include scientific ops\nelse: switch back to "standard"

CalculatorCLI -> User: show mode switch confirmation
deactivate CalculatorCLI

== Memory Retrieve Flow ==
User -> CalculatorCLI: --memory-retrieve flag
activate CalculatorCLI

CalculatorCLI -> MemoryService: retrieve()
activate MemoryService

MemoryService -> JsonStorage: load_memory_all()
activate JsonStorage
JsonStorage --> MemoryService: list[MemoryEntry]
deactivate JsonStorage

MemoryService --> CalculatorCLI: list[MemoryEntry]
deactivate MemoryService

CalculatorCLI -> User: display memory history
deactivate CalculatorCLI

== Memory Store Flow ==
User -> CalculatorCLI: --memory-store OP [--result R | --error MSG]
activate CalculatorCLI

CalculatorCLI -> MemoryService: store(entry)
activate MemoryService

MemoryService -> JsonStorage: save(memory_entry)
activate JsonStorage
JsonStorage --> MemoryService: saved
deactivate JsonStorage

MemoryService --> CalculatorCLI: done
deactivate MemoryService

CalculatorCLI -> User: confirm stored
deactivate CalculatorCLI

== Filter Flow ==
User -> CalculatorCLI: --filter-op OP [--filter-state STATE] or interactive menu
activate CalculatorCLI

CalculatorCLI -> MemoryService: filter_entries(operation, state)
activate MemoryService

MemoryService -> JsonStorage: load_memory_all()
activate JsonStorage
JsonStorage --> MemoryService: list[MemoryEntry]
deactivate JsonStorage

MemoryService -> FilterService: filter_entries(entries, operation, state)
activate FilterService
FilterService --> MemoryService: filtered list[MemoryEntry]
deactivate FilterService

MemoryService --> CalculatorCLI: filtered results
deactivate MemoryService

CalculatorCLI -> User: display filtered entries
deactivate CalculatorCLI

== Statistics Flow ==
User -> CalculatorCLI: --statistics flag or interactive menu option
activate CalculatorCLI

CalculatorCLI -> StatisticsService: compute_statistics()
activate StatisticsService

StatisticsService -> MemoryService: retrieve()
activate MemoryService

MemoryService -> JsonStorage: load_memory_all()
activate JsonStorage
JsonStorage --> MemoryService: list[MemoryEntry]
deactivate JsonStorage

MemoryService --> StatisticsService: list[MemoryEntry]
deactivate MemoryService

note over StatisticsService: compute operation counts\ncount errors\ncalculate error rate\ncompute average execution time

StatisticsService --> CalculatorCLI: Statistics object
deactivate StatisticsService

CalculatorCLI -> User: display statistics
deactivate CalculatorCLI

== Export History Flow ==
User -> CalculatorCLI: --export-history FILE or interactive menu option
activate CalculatorCLI

CalculatorCLI -> MemoryService: export_history(filepath)
activate MemoryService

MemoryService -> JsonStorage: load_memory_all()
activate JsonStorage
JsonStorage --> MemoryService: list[MemoryEntry]
deactivate JsonStorage

MemoryService -> HistoryExportService: export_history(entries, filepath)
activate HistoryExportService

note over HistoryExportService: serialize entries to dict\nwrite JSON file

HistoryExportService --> MemoryService: done
deactivate HistoryExportService

MemoryService --> CalculatorCLI: done
deactivate MemoryService

CalculatorCLI -> User: confirm export
deactivate CalculatorCLI

== Import History Flow ==
User -> CalculatorCLI: --import-history FILE [--overwrite] or interactive menu option
activate CalculatorCLI

CalculatorCLI -> MemoryService: import_history(filepath, overwrite)
activate MemoryService

MemoryService -> HistoryExportService: import_history(filepath, skip_duplicates, existing_ids)
activate HistoryExportService

note over HistoryExportService: read JSON file\nvalidate structure\ndeserialize entries\ncheck for duplicates

HistoryExportService --> MemoryService: (entries, errors)
deactivate HistoryExportService

MemoryService -> JsonStorage: save(entry) [for each entry]
activate JsonStorage
JsonStorage --> MemoryService: saved
deactivate JsonStorage

MemoryService --> CalculatorCLI: (count, errors)
deactivate MemoryService

CalculatorCLI -> User: show import results
deactivate CalculatorCLI

@enduml
